            "name": "Get JsonModel for Create BGD"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774948040326"
          },
          "code": "GET_JSONMODEL_FOR_CREATE_BGD",
          "id": "1774948312828",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774948312830_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Given the user's request: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, chat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nand the summarized context: {{$context.$nodes.BGD_CREATE_AGENT_CONTEXT.$output}}\n\nHere are the published account segments: {{$context.$nodes.GET_BGACCOUNT_SEGMENTS_CREATE.$output}} \nBuyer roles: {{$context.$nodes.GET_BUYER_ROLES_CREATE.$output}}\npersona segments: {{$context.$nodes.GET_BGPERSONA_SEGMENTS_CREATE.$output}} \nbehavior segments: {{$context.$nodes.GET_BGBEHAVIORAL_SEGMENTS_CREATE.$output}} \n\nThere can be multiple persona, account and behavior segments, that's why we have an array. Never miss any of the following fields:\n\nJsonModel will have payload structure like this:\n{\n  \"profile\": {\n    \"buyingGroupProfileName\": {{$context.$nodes.GET_CREATE_BGD_NAME.$output}} ,\n    \"buyingGroupProfileDescription\": <Appropriate brief BGD description>,\n    \"productId\": {{$context.$nodes.EXACT_PRODUCT_FOUND.$output}},\n    \"productName\": <Name of the product>\n  },\n  \"criteria\": {\n    \"personaSegment\": [\n      {\n        \"segmentId\": <persona segment Id>,\n        \"SourceBuyer_RoleID\": <Source Buyer role id of the chosen buyer role from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"buyerRoleName\": <Buyer role name from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"description\": <Persona segment description>,\n        \"name\": <Persona segment name>,\n        \"buyerRolePriority\": <buyerRolePriority from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"buyingGroupBuyerRoleID\": <Buyer role id of the chosen buyer role from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"mcpsQueryRef\": <from persona segment call>\n      },\n      ....\n    ],\n    \"behaviorSegment\": [\n      {\n        \"segmentId\": <behavior segment Id>,\n        \"SourceBuyer_RoleID\": <Source Buyer role id of the chosen buyer role from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"buyerRoleName\": <Buyer role name from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"description\": <behavior segment description>,\n        \"name\": <behavior segment name>,\n        \"buyerRolePriority\": <buyerRolePriority from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"buyingGroupBuyerRoleID\": <Buyer role id of the chosen buyer role from Buyer roles api call>,\n        \"mcpsQueryRef\": <from behavior segment call>\n      },\n      ....\n    ],\n    \"accountSegment\": [\n      {\n        \"segmentId\": < account segment Id>,\n        \"description\": <account segment description>,\n        \"name\": <account segment name>,\n        \"mcpsQueryRef\": <from account segment call>\n      },\n      ....\n    ]\n  },\n  \"activationAttributes\": {\n    \"tenantID\": {{$context.$nodes.GET_TENANT_ID.$output.result}},\n    \"profileStatus\": \"Active\",\n    \"accountStatus\": \"Current\",\n    \"sourceProductID\": <Remove Fusion_ from {{$context.$nodes.EXACT_PRODUCT_FOUND.$output}}>,\n    \"distinguisher\": \"26c\"\n  }\n}\n\nYour job is to make jsonModel json string that will be used in the BGD create payload. Output nothing else other than this valid json string."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
